// The explicit trust boundary (design.md "What is not checked").
//
// Six members, all compiler built-ins, each one a promise the compiler cannot
// check: `raw_data`, `string_view` and `cstring_view` discard or manufacture
// provenance, `transmute` reinterprets bits, `forget` suppresses cleanup, and
// `free` releases storage nothing traced. This file is the whole package -- the
// visible import is the review mechanism.
//
// # `forget(value)`
//
// Consumes an owning value and runs no cleanup hook, for it or for anything it
// owns transitively: the resource is deliberately leaked, or relinquished to
// whatever owns it now. It is not a lifetime extension -- a borrow of the
// operand dies here exactly as it would at a `drop` -- so a place is written
// `forget(move(place))` and a temporary is passed directly.
//
// # `free(pointer)` and `free(pointer, allocator)`
//
// Releases an allocation the compiler cannot follow back to the `new` that made
// it: one reached through a `rawptr`, a parameter, or foreign code. It checks
// nothing. That the pointer is that allocation's base, that the allocator is
// the one that created it, that nothing still refers to it, and that this
// happens once are all the caller's.
//
// The operand is still a checked `^mut T`, because the release is *sized*: a
// pointer that travelled as a `rawptr` is cast back to the pointee type at the
// call, and that cast is what supplies the size and alignment to release. A
// handle over an opaque control block, `shared(T)` among them, has no other way
// to release it.
//
// # `transmute(T, value)`
//
// Reads the storage of `value` as a `T`, with no addressable operand — the
// pointer cast `(^T)(&value)^` written as one expression. The compiler checks
// the shape of the conversion and nothing else: the source and destination are
// the same size, and both have a trivial lifecycle. A managed value, a `^T`, a
// slice, a view, or a `dyn` is rejected on either side, as is an aggregate
// containing one: a bit cast may neither duplicate an owning representation nor
// hand back a borrow nothing loaned.
//
// Everything else is the caller's obligation. Producing a valid destination
// representation is not checked at runtime; a *constant* pattern that is not a
// value of the destination type at all — a `bool` outside `{0, 1}`, an enum
// with no such member, a `rune` outside the scalar range — is a compile error
// instead, since there is no caller left to hold responsible. A scalar integer,
// float, `bool`, `rune`, or enum result folds when its operand is constant,
// which is how a package builds an infinity or a NaN: neither has a literal
// spelling.
//
// Pointer destinations are `rawptr` and C pointers only, and the result is
// unchecked: dereferencing it is valid only when the bits already describe
// suitably aligned, live storage of the destination pointee type.
@(public)
package unsafe;
